                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a neat little game developed by students from a game-school in Montréal, Canada. It's not a completely polished project up to professional standards, but it comes close and it is defitinely a lot better than most of the low-cost thrash that floods Steam these days.\n\nThe idea behind it definitely works: progress through the levels of a 2D-platformer by using two different skins and solve some very easy puzzles in doing so. Combat feels a bit clunky, sounds aren't always present and the music gets repetitive very soon. But the idea is good, graphics are fine and animations show real promise. A fine example of what students at modern-day gaming schools are able to accomplish: more than a lot of those scam-developers who flood Steam with their thrash.",
